  "title": "Why has my renewal premium increased?",
  "metaDescription": "&nbsp;This is your blog post. Blogs are a great way to connect with your audience and keep them coming back. They can also be a great way to position yourself",
  "h1": "Why has my renewal premium increased?",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Our Recent Posts"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Am I covered for dental and optical treatment?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "How do I get pre-authorisation for a planned procedure?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "How does The Insurance Concierge get paid?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Tags"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Premium increases at renewal are common in international health insurance and are driven by a combination of factors."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Age Loading"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "As you get older, your premium increases because the statistical likelihood of making a claim rises. Most insurers apply age-band increases at renewal, typically every five years."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Medical Inflation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Healthcare costs rise every year. International medical inflation typically runs at 8 to 12% annually, which is reflected in renewal premiums industry-wide."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Claims History"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you or your dependants made significant claims during the policy year, some insurers apply a claims-related loading at renewal. However, BUPA Global, Allianz, and several other insurers on our panel operate community-rated pricing — meaning individual claims history does not affect your personal renewal premium."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "What Can You Do?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "We can review your plan and compare alternatives to ensure you are getting the best value at renewal. In some cases, adjusting your deductible or removing underutilised modules can bring the premium back in line without sacrificing essential cover."
    }
  ],
